sequence-complete-ticket-error-state: a failed TPM2_SequenceComplete leaves the sequence intact

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 3, "Response Codes"): "The normal response for
any command is TPM_RC_SUCCESS. Any other value indicates that the command did
not complete and the state of the TPM is unchanged."

TPM2_SequenceComplete of a hash sequence adds the last data, ends the hash
(the hash state is consumed) and only then computes the hash-check ticket,
which can fail (TPM_RC_FW_LIMITED/TPM_RC_SVN_LIMITED when the hierarchy's
proof is unavailable). The failed command leaves the sequence object loaded
with an ended hash state (and possibly ticketSafe updated), so a later
TPM2_SequenceComplete or TPM2_SequenceUpdate on it uses the consumed state
(version 185 enters failure mode). The ticket's proof is now obtained before
the sequence is changed, so the error leaves the sequence unchanged, as in
tpm-rs. Found by differential fuzzing.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/HashHMAC/SequenceComplete.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/HashHMAC/SequenceComplete.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/HashHMAC/SequenceComplete.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/HashHMAC/SequenceComplete.c
@@ -29,6 +29,20 @@
     {
         // Get the hash algorithm before the algorithm is lost in TpmHash_HashEnd
         TPM_ALG_ID hashAlg = sequenceObject->state.hashState[0].hashAlg;
+        // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+        // the ticket's proof is checked before the sequence is changed ("the
+        // state of the TPM is unchanged" after an error, Part 3 "Response Codes").
+        if(in->hierarchy != TPM_RH_NULL
+           && (sequenceObject->attributes.ticketSafe == SET
+               || (sequenceObject->attributes.firstBlock == CLEAR
+                   && CryptoCommon_TicketIsSafe(&in->buffer.b))))
+        {
+            TPM2B_PROOF proof;
+            TPM_RC      proofResult = HierarchyGetProof(in->hierarchy, &proof);
+            MemorySet(proof.t.buffer, 0, sizeof(proof.t.buffer));
+            if(proofResult != TPM_RC_SUCCESS)
+                return proofResult;
+        }
 
         // Update last piece of the data
         CryptoCommon_DigestUpdate2B(&sequenceObject->state.hashState[0],
